{"type":"message","id":"b9a012f2","parentId":"ce6626f4","timestamp":"2026-06-04T04:20:32.889Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It appears that the `rm -rf` command is not recognized on this Windows system. Instead, we should use PowerShell commands to remove the files and directories.\n\nLet's clear the conflicting files using the appropriate PowerShell command:\n\n```powershell\nRemove-Item -Recurse -Force hello-world\\*\n```\n\nThis command will recursively delete all contents in the `hello-world` directory. Once this is done, I can run the `create-react-app` command again.\n```json\n{\"name\": \"exec\", \"arguments\": {\"background\": true, \"command\": \"Remove-Item -Recurse -Force hello-world\\*\"}}\n```\n\nLet me proceed with executing this command now.\n```json\n{\"name\": \"exec\", \"arguments\": {\"background\": false, \"command\": \"Remove-Item -Recurse -Force hello-world\\*\"}}\n```\n\nThis will remove the conflicting files and directories. Once that's done, we can create the React app again.\n```json\n{\"name\": \"exec\", \"arguments\": {\"background\": true, \"command\": \"npx create-react-app hello-world --template typescript\"}}\n```\nLet me execute this now.\n```json\n{\"name\": \"exec\", \"arguments\": {\"background\": false, \"command\": \"Remove-Item -Recurse -Force hello-world\\*\"}}\n```"}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen2.5:7b","usage":{"input":11746,"output":278,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12024,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1780546832887}}
